 "final_text_tail": "., dtype_equal=True)` on the new and stored categories. With integer stored categories and float new ones, that flag makes the comparison take a same-dtype fast path on mismatched dtypes. That path is what raises the low-level buffer type error. I didn't run anything to confirm it, and I made no changes. The fix is to drop `dtype_equal=True` so the comparison returns False and the \"different categories\" `ValueError` is raised.\n\n{\"files\": [\"pandas/io/pytables.py\"], \"functions\": [\"IndexCol.validate_metadata\", \"DataCol.validate_metadata\", \"AppendableTable.write_data_chunk\", \"Table._create_axes\"]}",
